/*****************************************************************************
    Rulings of record (all Tony; the full wording is in formsRecon Part 3 under the same headings)
*****************************************************************************/
What a form is (2026-11-05)
    Attributes are a little language. fill is a drawing command wearing an attribute dress: at layout, not at define, its method sets the fill colour.
    An attribute that names a field is spelled := (fill:=wall, font:=titleFont, color:=white, onClick:=). Plain = in a define is a value copy. Each form gets its := when it comes up for repair (SEQ 534).
    A forward reference in := refuses by name until a form needs one.
Inheritance, one rule (2026-11-11, SEQ 623 R0; narrows SEQ 622 R2 to box properties, which superseded the 2026-11-09 "fill, borders and such change the style in effect")
    Text properties inherit, box properties don't -- whether set as an attribute or in a style.
    Inherit: font, color, align, valign, italic.      Field only: fill, border, strokeColor, rounded, shadow, opacity.
    The style applies as the leftmost attribute; a box attribute after it overrides the style on that field only.
    The properties themselves (italic, shadow, opacity, rounded, text, colours, fonts, images) are ruled in Topics/drawing.
    MEASURED (styleScopeT, shadowT SH-6, opacityT OP-2): every one behaves so. A held style's (style:=) text properties reach children two levels down, and a child's own wins.
style:= is the only spelling (2026-11-11, SEQ 624 R0)
    style="name" (quoted) is retired. The floor refuses a style that is not held, by name, and the field then has no style. The fixtures were respelled.
setFrame's rerun (2026-11-11, SEQ 626 R1-R5; the strokes are in docs/setFrameRerunProposal.md)
    The frame's home is a field of its own outside the form, passed in setFrame's request. The definition is never written.
    With no frame given, the top field's declared x, y, width and height are the default (as ruled 2026-11-07).
    A parent with no down or across overlays its children, as the old GUI did. A child's declared x and y are measured from its parent.
    Stroke 4 (layoutFrame and the listener) waits until Tony sorts out listening.
Listening (2026-11-11, SEQ 622 R4)
    field=$other is respelled field=other (no $) in time, but listening is Tony's to sort out. Recorded; nothing changed.
Form issues (2026-11-11, SEQ 622 R1)
    Nothing is respelled out of existence pending an issue's resolution. A form's issues are noted below the bail() on that form.
Percent (2026-11-11, SEQ 622 R0)
    Percent stays: a setFrame rerun after a resize depends on it.
Style (2026-11-03, 2026-11-09)
    Style attributes may go directly on fields. A field starts with a copy of its enclosing field's style; its attributes are processed left to right, each changing the style in effect; the change is scoped to the subtree.
    By convention style:= comes first on the line. Attributes never change style implicitly.
    Drawing happens after every attribute is processed. What is built is a lookup (own, style, enclosing) that gives the same answers wherever the convention holds.
    Style resolution is written in jittable kant; it resolves as a tree in a pre-pass and paints as a forward-only stream (incant/designDocs, DisplayDesignHTML / StreamModel / StyleResolution).
Attributes
    Naming: camelCase, no dashes; the qualifier first and the thing last (topBorder, strokeColor, fillColor); a plain name is the default case.
    fill is not inherited. A bare number is in points (1/72 inch).
    Dropped: pad, onLayout, flex, center, fit=text, and the drop list at the foot of formsTable. Anything dropped and wanted later comes back then.
    flex also meant across: a form that drops flex writes across where it relied on it.
Events (2026-11-04) -- ruled on paper, not built
    Click actions use onClick:=. A click selects the field first. Own action, then attribute actions left to right. Bubbling stays; a member's parent is its enclosing field (built, merge 24beb5f0).
    Layout's mouseUp calls a kant extern. Firing is proved with a synthetic point and no window.
Form files (from docs/forms.md, retired into this file)
    A form is define-only, with stop() or bail() and free prose below it; IncantForms/Windows/tree is the reference shape.
    Long text uses the (...#) literal. Comments are // text, with no braces in an action body.
    initFORMs is gone: a form that still calls it stops silently at exit 0 (F-73). Its replacement is the two search lines; a correctly scrubbed form produces output.
    Help text lives in the dESCRIPTIONs registry; a field names its entry with describe.

